cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "editjumps: an independent reproduction of EvoFlows edit-flow sequence editing"
abstract: >-
  An independent reproduction of EvoFlows (arXiv 2603.11703), an edit-flow generative model over
  protein sequences that proposes insertions, deletions and substitutions on a template, built on
  Edit Flows (arXiv 2506.09018) over an ESM-2 trunk. Includes the corpus build, the trunk
  adaptation, the Section 4.2 baselines, and the evaluation harness the reported numbers come from.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Author(s)"
version: 0.0.1
repository-code: "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/editjumps-BA56"
keywords:
  - antibody
  - protein engineering
  - sequence editing
  - flow matching
  - ESM-2
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
references:
  # Surnames only: these are the author lists as recorded in docs/evoflow_reproduction.md.
  - type: article
    title: "EvoFlows: Evolutionary Edit-Based Flow-Matching for Protein Engineering"
    authors:
